          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-19431 tests: make sanity-pcc/40 more robust",
        "message": "LU-19431 tests: make sanity-pcc/40 more robust\n\nsanity-pcc.sh test_40 compares the time of a 1MB read after a\nbackground PCC attach against a synchronous attach, and allowed\nonly 1s of slack, so VM timing jitter could make the async case\nappear slower and fail the test.  Allow 2s of slack, and make the\nerror messages distinguish the two time checks.\n\nAlso add the llite.pcc_async_threshold(4) man page.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pcc\nFixes: 5be466e87304 (\"LU-10499 pcc: async attach in the background for PCC-RO file\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I92be5b3b99be48b40f1107250ae96016403ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
